Directory name is the architecture. A model is a config inside the one that
matches it, not a directory of its own.

  dense/     dense MLP, KV-cache attention
  moe_dsa/   MoE, sparse-selected KV attention        glm52, dsv4
  moe_swa/   MoE, sliding-window KV attention         mimo25
  moe_kla/   MoE, recurrent linear/delta state        qwen36, k3

The split that matters is the last one: moe_kla carries fixed-size state per
sequence and never grows a KV cache, so it pages differently, schedules
differently and shares no attention kernel with the other three. dsa and swa are
both attention over stored KV and differ in which keys they read.

Each directory holds:

  driver.cu    the device driver for this architecture
  plan.c       weight pack binding
  <model>.h    one header per model: shapes and constants only, no code

Two models in the same directory share driver.cu entirely. That is the point of
naming by architecture rather than by vendor: glm53 is a header, not a tree.
